== Where did the diagnostic reader fail?

Of Qwen's 51 false deletions, 47 occurred with 100% of the isolated silhouette exposed and four on the hidden pairs above. Twenty-nine occurred at the nominal camera pose. On 80 retained MuJoCo controls, the unmarked reference and revisit had identical RGB pixels within the same query. The scorer still marked the reference and constructed its crops. Both geometric methods correctly answered PRESENT on all 80. Qwen reported removal on seven. These controls isolate a failure that needs neither occlusion nor camera motion.

Among the 406 retained views with at least 99.95% exposure, false deletion was more frequent for smaller targets. Sorting by native silhouette area gave 33/135, 10/135 and 4/136 false deletions from the smallest to largest third. The comparison is descriptive. Target identity, layout, view and apparent size vary together.

We examined the shared registration gate after seeing the results. It admitted the same 834 queries for dense geometry and Qwen and stopped 446. Of 419 admitted removals, dense geometry found 399 and Qwen found all 419. Among 415 admitted retained targets, dense geometry reported two false deletions and Qwen reported 51. The dense rule had correctly answered PRESENT on 42 of the 49 additional errors. Qwen itself returned UNKNOWN on two admitted queries. As an exploratory check on the same inputs, calling removal whenever the dense match score fell below 0.60 detected all 419 removals with six false deletions. This binary check scores removal calls only. We chose it after inspecting outcomes. Its performance on fresh layouts is unknown.
